WEBVTT

00:00.711 --> 00:03.642
[jaunty ukulele music]
[欢快的尤克里里音乐]

00:03.711 --> 00:10.918
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

00:12.263 --> 00:13.884
- Why, you...
- 为什么，你...

00:13.953 --> 00:17.091
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

00:17.160 --> 00:19.160
- Why, you...
- 为什么，你...

00:19.229 --> 00:21.505
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

00:21.573 --> 00:23.987
- Why, you...
- 为什么，你...

00:24.056 --> 00:25.815
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

00:25.884 --> 00:28.229
- [laughing hysterically]
- [歇斯底里地大笑]

00:30.642 --> 00:31.711
- Wow!
- 哇！

00:31.780 --> 00:33.367
It's "The Sir Urchin
这就是《顽童先生》

00:33.436 --> 00:35.711
and Snail Fail Show"!
和蜗牛失败秀”！

00:35.780 --> 00:38.953
- It's cartoon time, SpongeBob!
- 海绵宝宝，卡通时间到了！

00:39.022 --> 00:41.987
SpongeBob?
SpongeBob?
海绵宝宝？
海绵宝宝？

00:42.056 --> 00:45.298
[ponderous orchestral music]
[沉闷的管弦乐]

00:45.367 --> 00:46.401
SpongeBob?
海绵宝宝？

00:46.470 --> 00:48.642
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

00:48.711 --> 00:50.298
SpongeRobert?
海绵罗伯特？

00:50.367 --> 00:53.367
- Oh!
- 哦！

00:53.436 --> 00:54.918
It's cartoon time!
卡通时间到了！

00:54.987 --> 00:57.298
I'll get our "Sir Urchin" hats.
我去拿我们的“顽童爵士”帽子。

00:57.367 --> 00:58.401
Whoa.
哇哦。

00:58.470 --> 01:00.815
- Not so fast, SpongeBob.
- 别那么快，海绵宝宝。

01:00.884 --> 01:03.125
What's in the secret room?
密室里有什么？

01:03.194 --> 01:04.711
- It's not a secret room,
Patrick.
- 这不是一个秘密房间，
帕特里克.

01:04.780 --> 01:06.401
It's my library.
这是我的图书馆。

01:06.470 --> 01:07.987
- W-what's that word mean?
- 这、这个词是什么意思？

01:08.056 --> 01:12.125
- A library is a... playground
for your mind.
- 图书馆是...游乐场
为了你的心意。

01:12.194 --> 01:14.711
- [vacant drone]
- [空置无人机]

01:14.780 --> 01:17.677
[laughter]
[笑声]

01:17.746 --> 01:19.608
Hm...
嗯...

01:19.677 --> 01:22.194
[laughs]
[笑]

01:22.263 --> 01:25.711
Let's do it!
It's library time!
我们开始做吧！
图书馆时间到了！

01:25.780 --> 01:30.091
- Ow!
Ow!
- 噢！
噢！

01:30.160 --> 01:31.780
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

01:31.849 --> 01:34.125
[ukulele music]
[尤克里里音乐]

01:35.884 --> 01:39.091
- [enthusiastic grunting]
- [热情的咕哝声]

01:41.091 --> 01:43.229
[yells]
[喊叫]

01:43.298 --> 01:44.918
- [meows]
- [喵]

01:44.987 --> 01:47.746
[hisses]
[嘶嘶声]

01:47.815 --> 01:50.056
- Oh, tender, naive Patrick,
-哦，温柔、天真的帕特里克，

01:50.125 --> 01:52.436
it's not that kind
of playground.
不是那样的
的游乐场。

01:52.505 --> 01:54.608
It's a place to read books!
See?
这是一个看书的地方！
看？

01:54.677 --> 01:58.229
- I love books!
- 我喜欢书！

01:58.298 --> 01:59.953
[laughing] Book!
[笑] 书！

02:00.022 --> 02:02.263
Book!
书！

02:02.332 --> 02:03.918
- Gary, I don't think
Patrick knows
- 加里，我不认为
帕特里克知道

02:03.987 --> 02:05.470
how to use a book properly.
如何正确使用一本书。

02:05.539 --> 02:06.505
Ow!
噢！

02:06.573 --> 02:10.022
[ukulele music]
[尤克里里音乐]

02:10.091 --> 02:12.091
Behold the books, Patrick.
看书吧，帕特里克。

02:12.160 --> 02:14.436
Each one has a story to tell.
每个人都有一个故事要讲。

02:14.505 --> 02:16.677
- Whoa.
- Look out!
- 哇哦。
- 小心！

02:16.746 --> 02:18.746
Those books are cliffhangers,
那些书都是扣人心弦的，

02:18.815 --> 02:20.780
stories for the adventurous.
适合冒险家的故事。

02:20.849 --> 02:21.815
- [pained grunt]
- [痛苦的咕哝声]

02:21.884 --> 02:23.298
[nervous yelling]
[紧张的叫喊]

02:23.367 --> 02:25.022
I'll save you!
我来救你！

02:25.091 --> 02:26.436
Whoa!
哇！

02:26.505 --> 02:29.401
[dramatic orchestral music]
[戏剧管弦乐]

02:29.470 --> 02:31.815
- There are logbooks,
- 有日志，

02:31.884 --> 02:36.332
unabridged books,
未删节的书籍，

02:36.401 --> 02:38.091
and books with bridges.
和有桥梁的书。

02:38.160 --> 02:39.677
- Whoa!
- 哇！

02:39.746 --> 02:41.505
[laughs]
[笑]

02:41.573 --> 02:43.470
- Listen to the soothing sounds
- 聆听舒缓的声音

02:43.539 --> 02:45.022
of the audiobooks.
有声读物。

02:45.091 --> 02:46.677
[seagulls crying]
[海鸥的哭泣]

02:46.746 --> 02:48.849
I can hear the ocean.
我能听到大海的声音。

02:48.918 --> 02:50.677
[toilet flushing]
[冲厕所]

02:50.746 --> 02:51.780
Me too!
我也是！

02:51.849 --> 02:53.125
[laughter]
[笑声]

02:53.194 --> 02:55.849
- Cookbooks,
for the culinarily curious.
- 食谱，
对于对烹饪感兴趣的人。

02:55.918 --> 03:01.849
- [vacant grunting]
- [空洞的咕哝声]

03:01.918 --> 03:03.746
I like the pictures.
我喜欢这些照片。

03:03.815 --> 03:06.229
- Ah, but the pictures
are a mere snack!
- 啊，但是照片
只是零食！

03:06.298 --> 03:09.401
It's the words in the book
that really feed your brain.
这是书上的话
这确实可以满足您的大脑需求。

03:09.470 --> 03:12.780
Let's start you off
with an old book.
让我们开始吧
与一本旧书。

03:12.849 --> 03:15.849
[light orchestral music]
[轻快的管弦乐]

03:15.918 --> 03:18.332
[eerie music]
[诡异的音乐]

03:18.401 --> 03:22.056
[sniffs]
Ah, musty old books smell.
[嗅嗅]
啊，旧书发霉的味道。

03:22.125 --> 03:25.642
Now read the words, Patrick.
现在读一下这句话，帕特里克。

03:25.711 --> 03:27.505
- Oh, read the--
- 哦，读一下——

03:27.573 --> 03:29.263
oh, uh...
哦，呃...

03:29.332 --> 03:30.298
"Once...
“一次...

03:30.367 --> 03:33.470
Upon a..."
经一...”

03:33.539 --> 03:34.470
"Once upon a"...
“从前”...

03:34.539 --> 03:36.298
Once upon a what?
从前什么？

03:36.367 --> 03:37.608
- To continue the story,
- 为了继续这个故事，

03:37.677 --> 03:39.539
you have to turn the page.
你必须翻页。

03:39.608 --> 03:40.849
- Oh.
- 哦。

03:40.918 --> 03:42.401
"Time."
“时间。”

03:42.470 --> 03:44.470
"Once upon a time"!
“曾几何时”！

03:44.539 --> 03:45.849
[laughs]
[笑]

03:45.918 --> 03:49.298
That's the most amazing trick
I've ever seen!
这才是最神奇的绝招
我见过！

03:49.367 --> 03:51.091
I want to stare
at more words!
我想凝视
更多的话！

03:51.160 --> 03:52.987
- Then feast your eyes!
-那就大饱眼福吧！

03:53.056 --> 03:56.194
[ethereal music]
[空灵的音乐]

03:56.263 --> 04:02.401
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:02.470 --> 04:05.642
Once upon a time...
曾几何时...

04:05.711 --> 04:10.436
- [quavering]
- [颤抖]

04:10.505 --> 04:12.194
Once a--
有一次——

04:12.263 --> 04:13.505
You're too slow!
你太慢了！

04:13.573 --> 04:14.711
[muttering]
[嘀咕]

04:14.780 --> 04:16.780
- He likes it!
Hey, Patrick!
- 他喜欢！
嘿，帕特里克！

04:16.849 --> 04:19.470
- [muttering]
- [嘀咕]

04:19.539 --> 04:21.263
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:21.332 --> 04:23.401
- [sniffing]
- [嗅嗅]

04:23.470 --> 04:25.815
[gasps]
[喘气]

04:25.884 --> 04:26.918
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:26.987 --> 04:28.746
[industrious grunting]
[勤奋的咕哝]

04:28.815 --> 04:36.022
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:38.229 --> 04:41.332
[dramatic orchestral music]
[戏剧管弦乐]

04:41.401 --> 04:44.091
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:44.160 --> 04:45.849
- Ooh, Patrick, your head
is absorbing
- 哦，帕特里克，你的头
很吸引人

04:45.918 --> 04:47.056
all the book knowledge,
书本上的所有知识，

04:47.125 --> 04:48.470
just like a sponge!
就像海绵一样！

04:48.539 --> 04:49.987
[laughs]
[笑]

04:50.056 --> 04:53.815
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:53.884 --> 04:55.849
[laughs]
Go, Patrick!
[笑]
去吧，帕特里克！

04:55.918 --> 04:57.298
Get those words!
明白这些话！

04:57.367 --> 04:58.815
Get them good!
让他们好起来！

04:58.884 --> 05:06.091
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

05:11.091 --> 05:13.780
- Stop reading words!
- 别再读文字了！

05:13.849 --> 05:17.125
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

05:17.194 --> 05:19.298
- Wow, what a bookworm!
- 哇，真是个书呆子！

05:19.367 --> 05:20.539
Whoa.
哇哦。

05:20.608 --> 05:22.091
- Yes, SpongeBob?
- 是的，海绵宝宝？

05:22.160 --> 05:23.470
- Uh, Patrick, I think
- 呃，帕特里克，我想

05:23.539 --> 05:24.746
that's enough knowledge
for one day.
这些知识就足够了
一天。

05:24.815 --> 05:26.091
Looks like you're full.
看来你已经吃饱了

05:26.160 --> 05:28.573
- Nonsense, dear boy.
- 废话，亲爱的孩子。

05:28.642 --> 05:32.056
One can never accumulate
too much information.
一个人永远无法积累
太多的信息。

05:32.125 --> 05:33.918
[genteelly] Ahem.
[礼貌地]咳咳。

05:33.987 --> 05:35.401
- Well, we're fresh
out of books.
- 嗯，我们很新鲜
没有书了。

05:35.470 --> 05:37.125
Come on, I'll buy you
an ice cream.
来吧，我买给你
一个冰淇淋。

05:37.194 --> 05:39.194
- Ah, I must confess to feeling
- 啊，我必须承认这种感觉

05:39.263 --> 05:41.953
more than slightly peckish.
不仅仅是有点饿。

05:42.022 --> 05:44.022
- Patrick, I'm so proud of you!
- 帕特里克，我为你感到骄傲！

05:44.091 --> 05:46.677
Ooh, you're a big brain now!
呵呵，你现在脑子真大啊！

05:46.746 --> 05:48.505
- Ooh!
- 哦！

05:48.573 --> 05:52.780
Oh, a skosh too big, it seems,
eh, wha'?
哦，看起来太大了，
呃，什么？

05:52.849 --> 05:55.022
- "Eh, wha'" what?
- [laughs]
- “呃，什么”什么？
- [笑]

05:55.091 --> 05:57.401
Oh, no matter,
my plebeian friend.
哦，没关系，
我的平民朋友。

05:57.470 --> 05:59.884
I shall simply
exit posthaste,
我将简单地
匆忙退出，

05:59.953 --> 06:02.746
posterior-first.
后先。

06:02.815 --> 06:05.642
Oof!
钱币！

06:05.711 --> 06:08.056
- I got it.
- Careful.
- 我得到了它。
- 小心。

06:08.125 --> 06:09.642
- Little bit...
Wow.
- 一点点...
哇。

06:09.711 --> 06:12.022
You really got your melon
jammed in there, didn't you?
你真的得到了你的瓜
塞在那里，不是吗？

06:12.091 --> 06:13.953
- Oh, true, SpongeBob.
- 噢，是的，海绵宝宝。

06:14.022 --> 06:16.573
Eh, but we can easily
solve this problem
嗯，但是我们可以很容易地
解决这个问题

06:16.642 --> 06:19.298
on a quantum physics level.
Take this down.
在量子物理层面上。
把这个拿下来。

06:19.367 --> 06:21.815
If we reduce
my subatomic particles
如果我们减少
我的亚原子粒子

06:21.884 --> 06:24.298
by way
of orbital electromagnetism,
顺便
轨道电磁学，

06:24.367 --> 06:26.608
we'll create
a harmonic oscillation
我们将创造
简谐振动

06:26.677 --> 06:27.918
within the molecules,
分子内，

06:27.987 --> 06:31.505
resulting in
a wave-function collapse,
导致
波函数塌缩，

06:31.573 --> 06:34.780
which will enable
my "melon,"
这将使
我的“瓜”

06:34.849 --> 06:36.436
as you so drolly put it,
正如你滑稽地说的那样

06:36.505 --> 06:37.608
to slip out.
溜出去。

06:37.677 --> 06:39.608
- Okay, sure.
- 好吧，当然。

06:39.677 --> 06:42.401
Let's give it a try.
让我们尝试一下。

06:42.470 --> 06:46.642
[muttering]
[嘀咕]

06:46.711 --> 06:49.642
[otherworldly music]
[超凡脱俗的音乐]

06:49.711 --> 06:50.711
- [meows]
- [喵]

06:50.780 --> 06:51.711
- Gary!
- 加里！

06:51.780 --> 06:52.918
Speak to me.
跟我说话。

06:52.987 --> 06:55.022
Oh...
哦...

06:55.091 --> 06:56.091
- [meows]
- [喵]

06:56.160 --> 06:57.229
- Oh, Gary, you're back.
- 哦，加里，你回来了。

06:57.298 --> 06:59.263
I'd know that slime anywhere.
我会在任何地方都认识这种粘液。

06:59.332 --> 07:00.953
[gasps]
Slime!
[喘气]
史莱姆！

07:01.022 --> 07:03.642
That's it!
[laughs]
就是这样！
[笑]

07:03.711 --> 07:05.677
Slime it up, Gar-bear.
把它粘起来，加熊。

07:05.746 --> 07:07.642
- [laughs]
- [笑]

07:07.711 --> 07:09.918
Abominable.
可恶。

07:09.987 --> 07:13.229
- Yeah, that Gary grease
ought to do it.
- 是的，加里油脂
应该这样做。

07:13.298 --> 07:15.332
Okay, Patrick,
pull yourself out.
好吧，帕特里克，
把自己拉出来。

07:15.401 --> 07:18.608
[jaunty ukulele music]
[欢快的尤克里里音乐]

07:18.677 --> 07:21.677
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

07:21.746 --> 07:25.125
[yells]
[喊叫]

07:25.194 --> 07:28.505
Hey.
"Head Shrinking for Beginners."
嘿。
“初学者的头缩小”。

07:28.573 --> 07:29.815
Hm...
嗯...

07:29.884 --> 07:31.815
[energetic drum music]
【充满活力的鼓乐】

07:31.884 --> 07:33.815
[screams]
[尖叫声]

07:33.884 --> 07:36.401
[chicken clucks]
[鸡咯咯叫]

07:36.470 --> 07:38.677
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

07:38.746 --> 07:44.677
[chanting, yelling]
[口号、喊叫]

07:44.746 --> 07:49.642
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

07:49.711 --> 07:52.849
[chicken clucks]
[鸡咯咯叫]

07:52.918 --> 07:54.642
[high-pitched] Oh, I give up!
[高调]哦，我放弃了！

07:54.711 --> 07:57.780
I guess we'll have to live here
in the library forever, Gary.
我想我们得住在这里
永远在图书馆里，加里。

07:57.849 --> 07:59.470
- [meows]
- [喵]

07:59.539 --> 08:04.780
- [cries]
- [哭声]

08:04.849 --> 08:08.160
- SpongeBob,
your typically moronic attempt
- 海绵宝宝，
你典型的愚蠢尝试

08:08.229 --> 08:10.091
has given me the solution!
已经给了我解决方案！

08:10.160 --> 08:13.091
Perhaps because
I had to smarten up
也许是因为
我必须变得聪明起来

08:13.160 --> 08:15.298
to get stuck...
被困...

08:15.367 --> 08:18.780
- You'll need to dumb down
to get free!
- 你需要冷静下来
获得自由！

08:18.849 --> 08:20.229
- [laughs]
- [笑]

08:20.298 --> 08:23.608
Who's sporting
the big brain now, hm?
谁在运动
现在脑子很大，嗯？

08:23.677 --> 08:24.711
[laughs]
[笑]

08:24.780 --> 08:25.780
- All right, Patrick.
- 好吧，帕特里克。

08:25.849 --> 08:27.711
Let's get stupid!
让我们变得愚蠢吧！

08:27.780 --> 08:29.436
Yeah!
是的！

08:29.505 --> 08:32.642
[industrious ukulele music]
[勤奋的尤克里里音乐]

08:32.711 --> 08:35.746
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

08:35.815 --> 08:37.056
Electronics.
电子产品。

08:37.125 --> 08:44.367
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

08:47.539 --> 08:48.780
Whew.
呼。

08:48.849 --> 08:51.229
I hope this works.
- Ah.
我希望这能起作用。
- 啊。

08:51.298 --> 08:54.125
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

08:56.056 --> 08:57.539
- Why, you...
- 为什么，你...

08:57.608 --> 08:59.780
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

08:59.849 --> 09:01.677
- Why, you...
- 为什么，你...

09:01.746 --> 09:03.332
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

09:03.401 --> 09:05.539
- I'm sorry, dear boy,
- 对不起，亲爱的孩子，

09:05.608 --> 09:07.436
but watching
this mindless drivel
但正在观看
这种无意识的胡言乱语

09:07.505 --> 09:09.573
isn't affecting me
in the least.
没有影响我
至少。

09:09.642 --> 09:12.056
[vacant moan]
[空洞的呻吟]

09:12.125 --> 09:14.815
- We've got drool!
- 我们已经流口水了！

09:14.884 --> 09:16.815
Patrick, it's working!
帕特里克，成功了！

09:16.884 --> 09:19.022
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

09:19.091 --> 09:23.367
- This is insulting
my intelligence.
- 这是侮辱性的
我的智力。

09:23.436 --> 09:26.470
[laughing] And I adore it!
[笑]我喜欢它！

09:26.539 --> 09:32.229
[lower,
more enthusiastic laughing]
[降低，
笑得更热情了]

09:32.298 --> 09:35.022
[rumbling]
[隆隆声]

09:35.091 --> 09:38.642
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

09:38.711 --> 09:41.125
- Why, you...
- 为什么，你...

09:41.194 --> 09:43.677
- What I do?
- 我做什么？

09:43.746 --> 09:46.539
- [frightened noises]
- [惊恐的声音]

09:46.608 --> 09:49.608
[crashing sounds]
[碰撞声]

09:51.367 --> 09:52.746
- We did it, Patrick!
- 我们做到了，帕特里克！

09:52.815 --> 09:55.780
The mindless drivel
is destroying your knowledge!
无脑的胡言乱语
正在摧毁你的知识！

09:55.849 --> 09:59.987
- [laughs]
- [笑]

10:00.056 --> 10:03.056
[vacant laughter]
[空洞的笑声]

10:03.125 --> 10:06.022
[building orchestral music]
[构建管弦乐]

10:06.091 --> 10:12.815
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

10:13.746 --> 10:15.884
Whoops.
Here, Patrick.
哎呀。
在这里，帕特里克。

10:15.953 --> 10:17.677
You may need
this little fella.
您可能需要
这个小家伙。

10:17.746 --> 10:19.436
- [vacant groan]
- [空洞的呻吟]

10:19.505 --> 10:21.125
Huh?
啊？

10:21.194 --> 10:22.229
Ah.
啊。

10:22.298 --> 10:25.229
[ukulele music]
[尤克里里音乐]

10:25.298 --> 10:30.125
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

10:30.194 --> 10:32.815
- Well, Patrick,
this is where we came in.
- 好吧，帕特里克，
这就是我们进来的地方。

10:32.884 --> 10:34.125
Ready for some ice cream?
准备好吃冰淇淋了吗？

10:34.194 --> 10:35.987
- Boy, am I ever!
- 男孩，我曾经吗！

10:36.056 --> 10:38.711
Oof.
A book?
钱币。
一本书？

10:38.780 --> 10:40.505
I love books!
我喜欢书！

10:40.573 --> 10:41.711
[yells]
[喊叫]

10:41.780 --> 10:44.194
A book!
[laughs]
一本书！
[笑]

10:44.263 --> 10:46.125
- That's right, Patrick.
- 没错，帕特里克。

10:46.194 --> 10:47.711
Play nice
with the pretty squares.
玩得好
和漂亮的方块。

10:47.780 --> 10:51.160
Gary, this is really
one for the books, eh?
加里，这真的是
一本用于书籍，是吗？

10:51.229 --> 10:53.056
[laughs]
- [meows dully]
[笑]
- [闷闷不乐地喵喵叫]

10:53.125 --> 10:57.780
- [laughs]
- [笑]

11:01.884 --> 11:08.884
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

♪ ♪